FSF GNU C reload change of 1994-08-07 (Richard Kenner), applied to the
2.6.0 release for KF3's GAME units. ChangeLog of GNU C 2.6.3:

	* reload.c (push_reload): Make test in LOAD_EXTEND_OP case more
	precise; handle CLASS_CANNOT_CHANGE_SIZE.
	(find_relods): When setting force_reloads, make LOAD_EXTEND_OP
	case more precise.

	* reload1.c (eliminate_regs, case SUBREG): Add USE of pseudo
	so we don't improperly delete an output reload.

Each new line is copied from GNU C 2.6.3, where no later ChangeLog entry
touches them. Left out: the CLASS_CANNOT_CHANGE_SIZE parts of the entry
(MIPS does not define that macro, so they compile to nothing) and all later
reload changes (1994-08-08 BYTES_BIG_ENDIAN test, 1994-09-21 eliminate_regs
LOAD_EXTEND_OP test).

Effect: a narrow read of a spilled word pseudo loads the narrow part from
the stack slot (`lhu`) instead of reloading the word (`lw` + use).

